{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And a woman when her flux flows.</b> To include the case of coercion." "<b>Her blood.</b> On account of herself, and not blood on account of the fetus." "<b>Many days.</b> But are they not only three days? Rather, since she separates from her husband and they are days of distress, it calls them many." "<b>Beyond her menstrual period.</b> Like 'with her menstrual period,' after the pattern of ״על שדה הארץ יחשב״ (it is reckoned upon the field of the land)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:12:33.397326433Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}